// ── Oracle sub-site canonicals (2026-09-09) ────────────────────────────────
// An Oracle tenant lists the same requisition on several career sites, each a
// token above. Ingest stores a requisition ONCE, under the best-ranked site
// that lists it (normalize.ts rankOracleSites / planOracleSubsiteVisit): rank 0
// is the site named here, else the tenant's first-listed site; the rest follow
// in catalog order. Only tenants whose first-listed site is NOT the right
// canonical need an entry. Every entry names a token present above; the
// oracle-subsite-dedupe test refuses one that does not.
//
// Measured live 2026-09-09 (anon list calls, exact totals per token):
//   Cummins  fa-espx-saasfaprod1: CX_3001 "Technicians" is listed first and is
//            the largest (707) by one row, but it is an AUDIENCE view; CX_1006
//            "All Functions" (706) is the tenant-wide site and holds every req
//            the other views hold bar one. Canonical = All Functions.
//   eexs     "All" (CX_3001, 641) is first-listed and canonical, but it is NOT
//            a superset of "All Community" (CX_11009, 455): 19 of 78 reqs in
//            a 7-day window were unique to All Community. The rank rule keeps
//            those under All Community automatically; no override needed —
//            recorded here so nobody removes All Community as "a duplicate".
//   Clean Harbors epyc, Hearst eevd, Tremco hcwx: the first-listed site is the
//            English/corporate site and already canonical; their measured pure
//            mirrors (FR site, "(inactive)" site, duplicate "Hearst") were
//            REMOVED from the catalog above rather than fetched for nothing.
//   Coherent hcwp, RPM brands hcwx, Chartwell hcrw, Penske fa-euyk, Tenet eodr:
//            sub-sites carry their OWN requisitions (0 overlap measured) — the
//            rank rule stores each once under its own site, nothing to override.
